# FINDING 1 (primary) — removable authorization control on `trainings`

**File**: `pb_hooks/trainingslib.js` line **395**, flags computed at **387-388**.

```js
387:  var isCancelTransition = !original.getBool('is_cancelled') && record.getBool('is_cancelled');
388:  var isRestoreTransition = original.getBool('is_cancelled') && !record.getBool('is_cancelled');
...
394:  // --- IDOR (C-6): обычный пользователь — только себя; посещаемость — только модератор ---
395:  if (!isCancelTransition && !isRestoreTransition) {
396:    if (added.length && !isModerator) { ... 'Можно записать только себя' ... }
403:    if (removed.length && !isModerator) { ... 'Можно снять с записи только себя' ... }
410:    if ((attendedAdded.length || attendedRemoved.length) && !isModerator) {
411:      throw new ForbiddenError('Отметка посещения — только модератор');
412:    }
413:  }
```

**Root cause**: `isCancelTransition`/`isRestoreTransition` derive from the **request body** field
`is_cancelled`. A `user`-role caller chooses whether the authorization block executes. Both the
`attended_users` check (moderator-only) and the self-only checks are skipped whenever the same
request flips `is_cancelled`.

**Reachable write** — restore branch, `pb_hooks/trainingslib.js:489-493`:
```js
489:        record.set('unpaid_booked_users', restoreUnpaid);
490:        for (i = 0; i < restoreAttended.length; i++) {
491:          adjustAttendanceCountTx(txApp, restoreAttended[i], 1);
492:        }
```
`adjustAttendanceCountTx` (`:266-276`) sets `users.attendance_count` + `app.save` with **no authz**.
Inside `runInTransaction` the save does not re-enter `onRecordUpdateRequest`, so the `users` field
ACL (`pb_hooks/users_access_guard.pb.js:15-33`) is **not** a second layer.

**Why the sibling ACL misses it** — `assertTrainingUpdateAllowed` (`:359-372`) uses
`TRAINING_USER_EDITABLE` (`:304-310`) = {booked_users, unbooked_users, unpaid_booked_users,
moderator_kicked_users, restore_insufficient_users}. `attended_users` is in
`TRAINING_COMPARE_FIELDS` (`:312-318`) but **not** in the editable map ⇒ rejected only while line 395
lets the block run. Both controls gate on the same attacker-chosen predicate ⇒ they fail together.

**LIVE EVIDENCE** (user token, training `qs808160ey9ib5q`; Caido proxy adds intermittent 502s for
identical bodies, so every result below reproduced on repeat):
```
{"booked_users":["<self>"]}                      -> 200   (newlyAdded == [])
{"booked_users":["<self>","aaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"]}    -> 403   {"message":"Можно записать только себя"}
{"attended_users":["<self>"]}                    -> 403   {"message":"Изменение поля \"attended_users\" недоступно."}
{"is_cancelled":true,"attended_users":["<self>"]}-> 403   {"message":"Изменение поля \"is_cancelled\" недоступно."}
{"date":"2026-08-27 12:30:00.000Z"}              -> 403   "date"
{"location":"HACKTEST"}                          -> 403   "location"
{"is_deleted":true}                              -> 403   "is_deleted"
{"is_closed":true}                               -> 200
```
Rows 1-2: only the arrival of a new id differs ⇒ `applyBookingSideEffects` **executes** and the
self-only check is the **live gate**. Rows 3-4: the guard ran and reported the *unrelated* field
`is_cancelled` instead of `attended_users` ⇒ it never evaluated the attendance change.

**REGRESSION (git)**: `git show 5ea0b5b:pb_hooks/trainingslib.js` (v0.39) already has the identical
wrapper + the same restore-branch `adjustAttendanceCountTx(+1)`. Commit `efaa612` (v1.0.18) is the
only commit touching this hook; its whole change adds `assertTrainingUpdateAllowed` in front of the
existing function — the derived-flag precondition was never touched.

**SEVERITY: Low (honest)**. `hasTimeRangeEnded(2026-08-26 12:30Z + 90min)` == true now, so line 473
`if (!ended)` skips the counter adjustment for the only training this token can see. 25 consecutive
cancel attempts (`{"is_cancelled":true,"booked_users":[]}`) gave 403/502, never 200 (a no-change
body gave 200 immediately). `attendance_count` was **never observed moving from 0**.
CVSS AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N. Confidence high for the control failure; the persisted
increment is an OPEN PROOF GAP (needs a not-yet-ended training).

**FIX** — make the checks transition-independent and add a set-based attendance comparison:

`pb_hooks/trainingslib.js:385` (after `var authId`):
```js
  var attendedUsersChanged = false;
  try {
    var originalAttended = audit.newlyAdded([], original.get('attended_users'));
    var recordAttended = audit.newlyAdded([], record.get('attended_users'));
    originalAttended.sort(); recordAttended.sort();
    attendedUsersChanged = originalAttended.join(',') !== recordAttended.join(',');
  } catch (_) { attendedUsersChanged = true; }
```

`pb_hooks/trainingslib.js:394-413` → replace with:
```js
  if (!isModerator) {
    for (i = 0; i < added.length; i++) {
      if (String(added[i]) !== authId) throw new ForbiddenError('Можно записать только себя');
    }
    for (i = 0; i < removed.length; i++) {
      if (String(removed[i]) !== authId) throw new ForbiddenError('Можно снять с записи только себя');
    }
    // Посещаемость — только модератор, включая cancel/restore.
    if (attendedUsersChanged || attendedAdded.length || attendedRemoved.length) {
      throw new ForbiddenError('Отметка посещения — только модератор');
    }
  }
```
`node --check` on the patched block: PARSE OK. Gates 1/2/3 reasoned (no local goja runtime);
Gate 4 = syntax only (no server-side tests exist under `pb_hooks/`).
